    "narrative":  "All twelve newly analyzed claims are valid, have adequate cell counts, and use the pre-specified signed direction. I used approximate 10% clinical benchmarks based on absolute outcome means: about 0.025 for most central dependency scores, about 0.0093 for outcome_006, and about 0.027 for outcome_013. Most new effects are not clinically or statistically supported. H21, H22, H33, H34, H35, and H38 are rejected: their intervals either do not reach the relevant clinical threshold or the signed estimate is opposite the hypothesized direction with no meaningful evidence in the registered direction. H30 is rejected for the directional hypothesis on outcome_006: feature_034=1 versus 0 shows a small opposite signed estimate, even though the interval is wide enough to include positive values. H19, H20, and H36 are left unresolved but deferred: their signed estimates are small and intervals cross zero, with upper bounds only modestly above the approximate threshold, so they do not justify validation or active follow-up. The only near candidates are the rare-absence binary markers H37 and H39. H37 has a signed estimate of +0.0253, about 9.4% of outcome_013's absolute mean, close to the clinical threshold, with a CI from -0.0016 to 0.0522. H39 has a signed estimate of +0.0232, about 9.1% of outcome_009's absolute mean, with a CI from -0.0023 to 0.0488. Neither discovery interval excludes zero, and neither point estimate itself reaches 10%, so I do not accept either on discovery evidence. However, both are near statistical and clinical relevance and could be real but noisy associations. I request independent validation for H37 because it is closest to the clinical threshold and closest to excluding zero. I keep H37 and H39 active and register cross-outcome follow-up tests for both markers to assess internal consistency. These remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
    "research_notes":  "Iteration 3 appraise after new batch: feature_060 track remains closed. Categorical contrasts H19-H22 and focused outcome refinements H33-H35 are mostly null. Rare-absence markers feature_047=0 versus 1 on outcome_013 and feature_023=0 versus 1 on outcome_009 are near threshold but not significant. Requested validation for H37. Keep H37 and H39 active; H19, H20, H36 unresolved but deferred; reject/closed H21-H22, H30, H33-H35, H38. Next follow-up: if validation supports H37, consider accepting if validation plus discovery evidence supports a >=10% clinically meaningful dependency-enhancing association; if validation fails, reject H37. H39 remains active pending internal-consistency tests or scheduled validation. Registered cross-outcome follow-ups: feature_047 absent versus present on outcome_009, and feature_023 absent versus present on outcome_013. All conclusions remain in-dataset associations only.",
